From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: attrr <110731994+attrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:00:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: qcom: sm8150: keep QUP0 and CO1 alive

Nothing on sm8150 votes for the QUP masters' BCM, nor for the NPU's:
once synced, with their initial bandwidth gone, the serial engines
froze the SoC (touch, I2C and all, no reset) and the NPU's BCM reset it
about a second later. Keep both at their minimum while awake, as the
other keepalive BCMs; the sleep set still drops them.

Workaround: nothing on sm8150 votes for the QUP masters' or the NPU's BCM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8150.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8150.c b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8150.c
index 4b0ee0409391..c9bb020a52d1 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8150.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8150.c
@@ -1378,7 +1378,7 @@ static struct qcom_icc_bcm bcm_sn1 = {
 
 static struct qcom_icc_bcm bcm_co1 = {
 	.name = "CO1",
-	.keepalive = false,
+	.keepalive = true,
 	.num_nodes = 1,
 	.nodes = { &qnm_npu },
 };
@@ -1445,7 +1445,7 @@ static struct qcom_icc_bcm bcm_cn0 = {
 
 static struct qcom_icc_bcm bcm_qup0 = {
 	.name = "QUP0",
-	.keepalive = false,
+	.keepalive = true,
 	.num_nodes = 3,
 	.nodes = { &qhm_qup0, &qhm_qup1, &qhm_qup2 },
 };
